Nalgene® is a polycarbonate formed from the diol **P** and $\text{COCl}_2$.

{{figure:pdf_visual_02.png}}

Draw **one** repeat unit of Nalgene®.

The cyclic peptide **B** is shown.

{{figure:pdf_visual_03.png}}

Cyclic peptide **B** is broken into its monomers by heating under reflux with dilute hydrochloric acid. The amino acid threonine, Thr, and two other organic products are formed.

{{figure:pdf_visual_04.png}}

Draw the structures of the two other organic products formed.
